;; Spike S5, S5-Q5: what ImageIO needs in S4's renderer profile
;; (spikes/s4/sandbox/profiles/renderer.sb). `s5-image --profile
;; renderer+imageio` appends this file to that profile. The rule was found by
;; S4's method: a crash or a logged denial, then the decoded pixels compared
;; with an unsandboxed run. tools/s5-measure.sh repeats its removal test.
;;
;; R1 (2026-10-18). Before decoding, ImageIO asks whether out-of-process
;; decoding is enabled for the application (IIOIsOOPEnabled, ApplicationOptIn),
;; which reads the main bundle's Info dictionary. Without metadata access to
;; the executable's directory, CFBundleGetMainBundle returns NULL inside the
;; profile and ImageIO dereferences it: SIGSEGV in __CFCheckCFInfoPACSignature
;; (observed on macOS 27.2, build 26B5112a). The rule reveals one directory's
;; metadata: not its listing, and no file's contents.
(allow file-read-metadata (literal (param "EXECUTABLE_DIR")))
